docs {
  # POST /api/sales/ — Create sale with empty/null/missing vip_code

  Demonstrates optional `vip_code` mapping to `None`. Requires `Authorization: Token {{token}}`. Source: `travels/serializers.py:72-76` (`validate_vip_code` returns `None` for `""`/whitespace/`null`/missing).

  This file uses `vip_code: ""`. Variants that also succeed with `201` and `sale.vip_code=None` (`GET` returns `vip_code:null`):

  ```json
  { "vip_code": null }
  { "vip_code": "   " }
  // or omit vip_code entirely
  {
    "service_type": 1,
    "client_name": "John",
    "client_email": "john@example.com",
    "location": 1,
    "vehicle": 1
  }
  ```

  ## Status codes

  - `201 Created` — `vip_code` treated as `None`, sale created, `GET` `vip_code:null`
  - `401 Unauthorized` — only for non-empty invalid vip_code (see `post_create_invalid_vip_code.bru`)

  ## Response (201)

  ```json
  {
    "status": "success",
    "message": "Sale created successfully",
    "data": {
      "payment_link": "https://checkout.stripe.com/c/pay/..."
    }
  }
  ```

  ## Notes

  - Use this to test “no vip” flow without removing the key.
}
